WEBVTT

00:24.407 --> 00:27.387
We're way less efficient as a duo.

00:27.387 --> 00:28.847
Damn it!

00:31.097 --> 00:34.357
I thought Heal Mushrooms 
were basically a guaranteed drop,

00:34.797 --> 00:38.777
but we killed four Matango 
and didn't see a single one.

00:39.757 --> 00:43.317
Maybe Ruche's Lady Luck 
was doing something after all.

00:43.317 --> 00:47.597
It didn't seem like anyone else 
was going after Matangos.

00:48.327 --> 00:50.457
It was just a coincidence.

00:50.457 --> 00:51.917
She could've stayed

00:51.917 --> 00:56.207
if she hadn't demanded a cut
from selling the Blood-soaked Sword.

00:56.537 --> 00:58.267
Should we invite her back?

00:58.267 --> 00:59.877
Listen, Reiss.

00:59.877 --> 01:02.357
I have my dignity to preserve.

01:02.357 --> 01:05.897
I can't invite her back 
after everything I said.

01:05.897 --> 01:09.387
I'd rather die than ask her for anything.

01:12.867 --> 01:16.177
Fortunately, we've got plenty of 
money from selling that sword.

01:16.177 --> 01:18.187
There's no need to panic.

01:18.187 --> 01:22.717
We can take our time finding someone 
who gets it, even if they're low-level.

01:24.777 --> 01:28.187
<i>That</i> dungeon? Not a rank D or C one?

01:30.077 --> 01:31.967
Where is he? I don't see anything.

01:33.657 --> 01:34.627
What's going on?

01:34.627 --> 01:38.207
Maybe someone defeated 
a high-level monster.

01:38.467 --> 01:39.867
Him again?

01:39.867 --> 01:41.717
Aren't Patchwork Bears strong?

01:41.717 --> 01:43.037
I've seen him before.

01:43.037 --> 01:47.047
A fresh rank E and rank F?

01:47.047 --> 01:50.687
They beat the Angel's Playbox? 
The recommended level is 50!

01:56.357 --> 01:57.427
You're kidding, right?

01:57.427 --> 01:59.527
Th-They did what?!

02:36.437 --> 02:37.687
<b>Loading</b>

02:48.947 --> 02:50.247
<b>Loading</b>

03:01.587 --> 03:02.877
<b>Loading</b>

03:11.137 --> 03:11.887
<b>Loading</b>

03:13.387 --> 03:18.977
<b>Begin Adventure</b>

03:13.397 --> 03:18.977
<b>Begin Adventure</b>

03:30.277 --> 03:34.247
<b>Episode 10\h\h\h\h\hNegotiation</b>

03:30.957 --> 03:33.077
We weren't trying to beat the dungeon.

03:33.387 --> 03:37.017
The Dreamlord attacked us 
while it was Wandering.

03:37.017 --> 03:40.787
If you don't believe me, 
two other adventurers were involved.

03:40.787 --> 03:42.067
You can ask them.

03:42.597 --> 03:43.877
Very well.

03:44.517 --> 03:48.947
The city was offering a bounty 
for defeating the Angel's Playbox,

03:48.947 --> 03:51.007
so I'll confirm with them.

03:54.747 --> 03:58.967
<i>Bounties are sometimes placed on 
dungeons near cities and villages.</i>

03:59.727 --> 04:04.147
<i>Monsters tend to come out of dungeons 
that have been left alone for too long,</i>

04:04.557 --> 04:09.237
<i>and they can lead to
disasters in the area.</i>

04:10.347 --> 04:13.737
<i>A dungeon's recommended level depends 
on the region in which it appears,</i>

04:14.117 --> 04:20.217
<i>with a clear separation between 
low and high-level areas.</i>

04:21.437 --> 04:24.797
<i>Some believe it's caused by 
the mana flowing in the region,</i>

04:24.797 --> 04:32.197
<i>while others say it's the will ofAlxeros 
and beyond human comprehension,</i>

04:32.197 --> 04:34.127
<i>but nothing is known for certain.</i>

04:35.427 --> 04:40.437
<i>High-level adventurers tend to operate out 
of cities where dangerous dungeons appear.</i>

04:41.037 --> 04:44.797
<i>The pay is better, and it does 
more to serve the kingdom.</i>

04:46.187 --> 04:51.927
<i>Because of that, no one in Rondalm 
could beat the Angel's Playbox.</i>

04:52.487 --> 04:57.327
<i>Fearing the dungeon would be ignored, 
the mayor put a bounty on it.</i>

05:01.667 --> 05:04.607
A bounty, huh?

05:04.607 --> 05:07.337
I wasn't expecting one 
and didn't even look into it.

05:07.337 --> 05:09.047
How much is it?

05:09.047 --> 05:10.967
Ten million gold.

05:12.617 --> 05:14.967
Ten million?!

05:14.967 --> 05:17.467
Ten million gold, huh?

05:17.467 --> 05:19.767
We really appreciate that.

05:19.767 --> 05:26.567
I know I should be glad, but our drops 
have ruined my ability to react normally.

05:26.567 --> 05:28.937
Was it Lady Luck?

05:29.307 --> 05:33.857
Did they get a rare drop from 
a recommended level 50 Dreamlord?

05:34.147 --> 05:39.497
<i>That Elymas guy scouted Ruche 
as soon as he figured she had Lady Luck.</i>

05:34.477 --> 05:38.927
I didn't think your Lady Luck 
would apply to this, too.

05:39.497 --> 05:41.937
<i>Then they suddenly got a huge payday.</i>

05:41.937 --> 05:46.807
<i>They seem completely 
indifferent to 10,000,000 gold.</i>

05:46.807 --> 05:49.957
<i>Just how much money have they made?</i>

05:47.827 --> 05:49.957
I'm just lucky all the time.

05:49.957 --> 05:56.467
Also, you'll be promoted to rank D 
in accordance with guild regulations.

05:56.467 --> 05:59.967
You'll be jumping 
from rank F to D, Ms. Ruche.

05:56.467 --> 05:59.967
<b>Rank B</b>

05:56.467 --> 05:59.967
<b>Rank C</b>

05:56.467 --> 05:59.967
<b>Rank D</b>

05:56.467 --> 05:59.967
<b>Rank E</b>

05:56.467 --> 05:58.387
<b>Rank F</b>

05:56.927 --> 05:59.967
<b>Rank A</b>

05:58.507 --> 05:59.967
<b>Rank S</b>

06:00.387 --> 06:03.337
R-Ruche is rank D?

06:03.337 --> 06:08.667
It's not clear how, but she rose 
beyond our reach at some point.

06:05.967 --> 06:10.477
Ruche is rank D? Rank D? Ruche?

06:09.397 --> 06:10.477
Cline?

06:12.207 --> 06:13.857
What's gotten into you?!

06:13.857 --> 06:14.667
We did—

06:14.667 --> 06:16.027
Ruche!

06:16.027 --> 06:17.527
I'm sorry!

06:17.527 --> 06:19.077
I've mended my ways!

06:19.077 --> 06:21.287
Please come back!

06:21.557 --> 06:26.197
We can split the money from selling 
the Blood-soaked Sword evenly, okay?

06:32.717 --> 06:33.717
Pathetic.

06:35.077 --> 06:36.587
Let's go, Ruche.

06:36.587 --> 06:38.797
It'll take time to investigate.

06:38.797 --> 06:39.847
Okay.

06:42.847 --> 06:46.897
W-Wait! At least hear me out!

06:47.397 --> 06:49.157
Could you...

06:50.637 --> 06:53.197
Could you at least...

06:53.607 --> 06:54.847
Yikes.

06:57.607 --> 06:59.727
This place looks expensive.

06:59.727 --> 07:00.617
I'm excited.

07:01.497 --> 07:04.617
Thank you for waiting, sir.

07:05.357 --> 07:11.957
The promotions and bounty 
were happy accidents.

07:17.357 --> 07:22.927
<i>Our promotions to rank D 
raised our skill point cap to 45.</i>

07:23.297 --> 07:26.947
<i>The Fang of Smoldering Insanity 
skillbook is within reach, too.</i>

07:27.847 --> 07:30.487
<i>How should we farm money next?</i>

07:32.527 --> 07:36.097
Wh-What is it, Mr. Elymas?

07:36.097 --> 07:37.527
Oh, sorry.

07:37.527 --> 07:41.657
We're celebrating. 
I should focus on having fun.

07:41.657 --> 07:43.407
That's right.

07:43.667 --> 07:46.407
Let's have a fun time.

07:46.877 --> 07:49.287
Cheers!

07:55.127 --> 07:59.257
We said we'd order 
whatever we wanted today.

07:59.587 --> 08:04.717
I've always dreamed of having all I can 
eat at the Alchemist King's Stove.

07:59.927 --> 08:04.717
<b>Alchemist
 King's
Stove</b>

08:05.007 --> 08:07.727
Once I felt like I'd made it 
as an adventurer,

08:07.727 --> 08:10.437
I wanted to come here with my party.

08:10.437 --> 08:15.577
I thought I'd be here with 
Mr. Cline and Ms. Reiss, though.

08:16.067 --> 08:20.507
Did you forget that I paid you 
the bare minimum? Ungrateful!

08:20.507 --> 08:22.067
You most certainly did not!

08:24.327 --> 08:30.077
<b>King Crab and Black Truffle Sauce Pie</b>

08:25.827 --> 08:30.077
Their king crab and black truffle 
sauce pie costs 8,000 gold?!

08:30.077 --> 08:32.547
I didn't think it'd be this expensive.

08:32.547 --> 08:34.497
I nearly ordered one.

08:34.907 --> 08:37.897
Mr. Elymas, don't order 
anything from this page!

08:37.897 --> 08:41.217
Let's look for something under 4,000 gold!

08:41.217 --> 08:44.367
One king crab and black truffle 
sauce pie, please.

08:44.367 --> 08:45.407
What?!

08:44.367 --> 08:46.097
Yes, sir.

08:46.097 --> 08:48.517
A-Are you sure?

08:50.277 --> 08:52.587
<i>It must not have sunk in yet.</i>

08:53.167 --> 08:57.077
Here's your king crab 
and black truffle sauce pie.

09:09.987 --> 09:11.977
It's really good.

09:13.757 --> 09:15.687
I'm in heaven.

09:16.347 --> 09:18.567
This is good, too.

09:19.227 --> 09:20.647
I'm glad to hear that.

09:21.067 --> 09:25.717
We should discuss how to split 
the loot and gold we earned.

09:26.237 --> 09:29.727
First, do you want to use 
the skillbook, Ruche?

09:30.437 --> 09:34.187
I think it'd be worthwhile for you 
to have Intermediate Wind Magic.

09:34.467 --> 09:36.747
You're not going to use it?

09:36.747 --> 09:37.517
No.

09:37.517 --> 09:40.987
It's not bad, but I'd like to aim higher.

09:40.987 --> 09:42.857
I've already got a build in mind.

09:43.397 --> 09:45.307
Then I won't use it either.

09:45.307 --> 09:47.037
What? Are you sure?

09:47.037 --> 09:51.497
With this skill tree, you'll have 
an easy time finding a party for a while.

09:53.067 --> 09:57.037
But that would mean 
having different goals.

09:57.597 --> 10:01.047
I want to aim higher, too.

10:01.387 --> 10:06.797
Besides, it'd be sad 
to say goodbye so soon.

10:09.767 --> 10:12.047
Then we'll sell it.

10:12.047 --> 10:14.457
To be honest, that'll help a lot.

10:15.547 --> 10:17.767
Were you short on money?

10:18.247 --> 10:23.527
After subtracting various expenses, 
we earned about 57,000,000 gold.

10:24.357 --> 10:26.867
Just hearing the amount makes me dizzy.

10:27.237 --> 10:31.007
We'll split this 80/20, 
so you get 46,000,000 gold.

10:30.037 --> 10:31.787
<b>46,000,000G</b>

10:31.007 --> 10:31.787
What?!

10:32.167 --> 10:35.287
And I get 11,000,000 gold.

10:32.867 --> 10:35.287
<b>Ruche: 46,000,000G</b>

10:33.117 --> 10:35.287
<b>Elymas: 11,000,000G</b>

10:35.997 --> 10:40.167
Please! You won't regret it! 
Let's form a party!

10:40.167 --> 10:42.667
How about an 80/20 split?

10:42.927 --> 10:45.677
You'd get 80%, of course. 
I'm fine with 20%.

10:45.677 --> 10:48.597
That offer was still on the table?!

10:50.217 --> 10:51.737
What's going on?

10:52.557 --> 10:55.097
Ruche, everyone's looking at us.

10:53.077 --> 10:54.427
Are they fighting?

10:55.397 --> 10:57.767
Is 80/20 not good enough?

10:57.767 --> 11:00.227
No, I'm sorr—no, wait!

11:00.227 --> 11:04.227
There's no way I could 
ever accept that amount.

11:04.227 --> 11:07.587
Where did that 80/20 split come from?

11:07.587 --> 11:11.827
Most deals involve a split like that.

11:11.827 --> 11:15.327
In what universe?!

11:15.327 --> 11:19.327
You can't seriously expect me 
to accept 40,000,000 gold!

11:19.327 --> 11:24.717
I already can't thank you enough 
for raising my level this much!

11:23.457 --> 11:24.327
Ruche!

11:26.377 --> 11:29.737
I thought it was a fair split...

11:35.177 --> 11:38.087
It's called a Lucky Bird.

11:41.767 --> 11:45.607
<i>We still haven't agreed on
how to split the treasure.</i>

11:46.107 --> 11:51.107
<i>We decided to visit the Hall of 
Broken Grimoires to sell our items.</i>

12:07.797 --> 12:10.717
Well, well. You're back.

12:11.207 --> 12:15.717
With a sweet girl this time. 
Friend of yours?

12:15.717 --> 12:17.697
You'd better still have it.

12:17.697 --> 12:19.997
You don't trust me, do you?

12:19.997 --> 12:23.557
Of course I've still got
the Fang of Smoldering Insanity.

12:23.557 --> 12:26.107
I value my customers' trust.

12:28.227 --> 12:32.227
This shop has the item you want?

12:32.227 --> 12:34.237
She seems like a sweet girl.

12:34.537 --> 12:39.747
You're not planning to make her 
use that skillbook, are you?

12:40.047 --> 12:41.587
Don't be ridiculous.

12:41.587 --> 12:43.497
I would never do that.

12:43.867 --> 12:45.067
It's for me.

12:45.747 --> 12:52.257
Uh-huh. Either way, 
you're a freak if you want that.

12:53.927 --> 12:57.497
I came to have you appraise some items.

12:57.497 --> 13:06.357
Oh, really? You seem too smart 
to consider selling anything here.

13:16.547 --> 13:19.507
Well, this is a surprise.

13:19.507 --> 13:22.077
Two Dazzling Raana Decorative Blades.

13:23.187 --> 13:28.087
If I'd known you were such a big shot, 
I would've treated you like one.

13:28.087 --> 13:30.547
My mistake.

13:30.547 --> 13:32.587
I'm not interested 
in tedious negotiations.

13:33.717 --> 13:37.397
I'll sell them to you for 30,000,000 gold.

13:37.967 --> 13:40.477
Any less, and I'll take them 
somewhere else.

13:47.087 --> 13:51.487
You'll have a hard time getting 
30,000,000 gold at a legitimate shop.

13:52.037 --> 13:56.167
But here, no rumors will spread, and you 
won't have to worry about jealousy.

13:56.167 --> 14:00.997
You shouldn't take unnecessary 
risks for a little extra money.

14:01.697 --> 14:04.167
I'll give you 25,000,000 gold.

14:04.167 --> 14:06.497
<i>Th-This old woman...</i>

14:06.957 --> 14:10.737
<i>I said I didn't want to negotiate.</i>

14:12.517 --> 14:17.347
Mr. Elymas, she's not wrong.

14:17.677 --> 14:20.827
Twenty-five million gold
 is a lot of money.

14:20.827 --> 14:22.477
Don't be swayed, Ruche.

14:22.477 --> 14:25.357
She'll take advantage 
of any weakness we show.

14:28.077 --> 14:33.887
<i>Thirty million gold is a high price, and 
it'll be tough to get that anywhere else.</i>

14:34.557 --> 14:38.447
<i>Considering the risk, 
I could just sell them here.</i>

14:38.827 --> 14:43.957
<i>But if I let her control the conversation, 
she'll negotiate for even less.</i>

14:46.187 --> 14:48.147
I have gold from selling Magic Stones.

14:49.087 --> 14:53.207
I can hold onto the swords 
until I can get a good deal.

14:53.207 --> 14:58.757
Then I can't make you 
do anything. That's a shame.

14:58.757 --> 15:03.847
But that's not why 
you're really here, is it?

15:08.237 --> 15:11.127
I have a skillbook 
dropped by a Dreamlord.

15:12.157 --> 15:14.357
I'm thinking about using it,

15:14.997 --> 15:19.037
but if you'll give me a good price, 
I'll consider selling it.

15:19.037 --> 15:21.147
A skillbook?

15:22.847 --> 15:26.997
I can't believe you found one so quickly.

15:26.997 --> 15:34.717
You—no, the two of you might be 
known as heroes before long.

15:35.507 --> 15:40.137
I see. So you want to sell this here.

15:40.457 --> 15:44.637
<i>She's interested, 
but how much can I get her to pay?</i>

15:45.077 --> 15:48.537
The market price is 20,000,000 gold.

15:48.537 --> 15:52.937
I'd be taking a risk 
by buying this from you.

15:52.937 --> 15:57.947
The guild would only give you 
7,000,000 gold for it.

15:58.517 --> 16:04.447
You seem skilled, so I'll bump up the 
price since we might do business again.

16:04.987 --> 16:09.587
I'll buy it for 14,000,000 gold.

16:09.587 --> 16:13.087
And you'll put it up for sale 
at an absurd markup, right?

16:13.337 --> 16:16.817
It's easy to find a buyer 
for Intermediate Wind Magic.

16:16.817 --> 16:22.407
If you want to be friends, then I think 
you could give me 22,000,000 gold for it.

16:28.357 --> 16:29.777
Hot!

16:29.777 --> 16:31.147
You brat!

16:31.147 --> 16:34.517
You have no intention of using it, do you?

16:34.517 --> 16:37.777
Don't be so brazenly greedy!

16:37.777 --> 16:39.637
Who's the greedy one?!

16:39.637 --> 16:42.777
I'm offering to be a customer!

16:42.777 --> 16:46.037
You don't have to be so stingy!

16:42.777 --> 16:46.037
<b>Panic</b>

16:42.777 --> 16:46.037
<b>Panic</b>

16:49.887 --> 16:51.407
Um...

16:52.327 --> 16:53.927
Um, so...

16:53.927 --> 16:58.507
Mr. Elymas, how much is that Fang of 
Smoldering Insanity skillbook you want?

16:58.507 --> 17:04.257
What now, girl? 
You're interrupting our fun.

17:04.257 --> 17:10.017
The rare skillbook he wants 
costs 55,000,000 gold.

17:10.017 --> 17:13.897
The market price is only 
30,000,000 gold, though.

17:13.897 --> 17:16.097
She's definitely taking advantage.

17:17.077 --> 17:20.027
Fifty-five million gold...

17:20.347 --> 17:24.527
I thought I knew what to expect, 
but that's still so expensive.

17:27.227 --> 17:28.847
Excuse me, ma'am.

17:29.787 --> 17:31.977
I have an idea.

17:31.977 --> 17:39.047
Would you trade that skillbook and these 
items for the Fang of Smoldering Insanity?

17:39.047 --> 17:42.677
What? That's hardly a fair deal.

17:42.677 --> 17:45.427
That's what you interrupted us for?

17:45.427 --> 17:46.677
<i>No, wait.</i>

17:47.007 --> 17:56.967
<i>Getting rid of a skillbook no one wants 
for items that are easy to sell isn't bad.</i>

17:58.187 --> 18:01.847
<i>Ruche's deal is good for us, too.</i>

18:01.847 --> 18:05.157
<i>We'd keep the payout from 
the Magic Stones and slaying monsters,</i>

18:05.157 --> 18:07.547
<i>plus the Fang of Smoldering Insanity.</i>

18:09.477 --> 18:11.037
Girl.

18:11.717 --> 18:15.037
You shouldn't interrupt 
a merchant's business,

18:15.777 --> 18:19.547
but betting on a future hero 
isn't a bad idea.

18:19.927 --> 18:22.667
I accept those terms.

18:22.947 --> 18:24.677
You do?

18:24.677 --> 18:30.177
No, wait! Then you 
won't get your full share!

18:30.467 --> 18:32.587
It's fine.

18:32.587 --> 18:35.477
Think of it as a thank you 
present from me.

18:35.477 --> 18:38.977
Th-This is too much for a thank you.

18:39.277 --> 18:42.607
And we don't know 
if next time will go as well.

18:43.077 --> 18:46.237
What if we have to disband 
our party for some reason?

18:46.237 --> 18:47.737
Mr. Elymas.

18:49.407 --> 18:52.877
Are you planning to abandon me?

18:52.877 --> 18:56.867
I'm starting to think you're 
preparing for a clean break.

18:55.717 --> 18:59.787
I-I'm not, but just in case...

18:59.787 --> 19:02.377
Then there's no problem.

19:03.457 --> 19:10.387
Come on, ma'am. Let's trade 
before Elymas can say anything else.

19:10.387 --> 19:12.867
Good job convincing him.

19:12.867 --> 19:15.917
Hold on tight so he doesn't get away.

19:15.917 --> 19:16.717
What?!

19:20.827 --> 19:24.147
<i>Why are they getting along?</i>

19:37.827 --> 19:41.787
<b>Somewhere within the County of Edvaughn</b>

20:51.607 --> 20:53.327
How revolting.

20:54.637 --> 20:56.947
Lady Malice, that's enough!

20:56.947 --> 20:59.457
Lifeforce Transfer has ended!

21:00.957 --> 21:03.167
Her methods seem a bit savage.

21:03.167 --> 21:04.977
It's good EXP, but still...

21:04.977 --> 21:05.957
Right?

21:14.677 --> 21:17.177
<i>You may have been exiled,</i>

21:17.177 --> 21:20.027
<i>but you don't go down easily.</i>

21:20.027 --> 21:22.687
<i>I've known that since we were young.</i>

21:23.887 --> 21:29.147
I need to take my time with you.

21:30.787 --> 21:32.947
Isn't that right,

21:33.437 --> 21:36.517
my dear Elymas?

21:55.967 --> 21:59.467
<b>Translator:
Sho Stifler

Timer:
Krzysztof Kunc

Editor:
Salem Alabanza

Quality Control:
Gabriella Alabanza

Final Quality Control:
Sriram Gurunathan</b>

23:10.277 --> 23:15.937
<i>The Fang of Smoldering Insanity 
skillbook is finally mine!</i>

23:16.257 --> 23:19.677
<i>"Beware of those with this Skill Tree.</i>

23:19.677 --> 23:22.807
<i>Dragging his shattered body 
and letting his torn tail flutter,</i>

23:22.807 --> 23:27.297
<i>not even the God of Death dares 
approach his unstoppable rampage!"</i>

23:27.647 --> 23:30.267
<i>I've missed this 
unsettling descriptive text.</i>

23:31.567 --> 23:33.567
<i>Next time, "Inescapable Past."</i>

23:34.567 --> 23:37.507
<i>No, wait. I need to stay grounded.</i>
